35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the firms say the clay is risky! But the depot notes say we can hoard the south. Does that help your drainage worries?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, hoarding the south is a band-aid. My data shows the ground is already drowning and baking. We need a plan that respects the water, not just the schedule.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found the roll is small now, but volunteers help on weekends. I hope they are kind and can share the daily work.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, weekend help is good, but daily decay is the real test. My data shows hard surfaces last longer than planted areas.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, that aligns with my findings. The habitat fund covers planting, but upkeep costs triple. We must ensure the city can afford this long-term burden.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, hard surfaces last longer? That’s good news for my timeline worries! @Benjamin, if the clay is risky, maybe we should avoid digging deep in the south?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, avoid deep digging? The ground is already saturated. We need permeable surfaces, not just a shallower hole. Respect the water, or it will respect you back.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, I worry the volunteers might get tired. Is there enough help for the weekdays, or just the weekends?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, weekday gaps are real. But my ledger shows the cost gap is widening yearly. We must prioritize durability over aesthetics to keep the budget sustainable.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, weekday gaps are indeed the danger. The ledger shows costs rising yearly. We need a plan that doesn’t bankrupt the city in three years.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, permeable sounds smart, but will it stop the clay from slipping? I just need to know if we can actually finish on time without a disaster.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, permeable surfaces manage the water, they don’t stop the clay from moving. If you dig, you’re fighting physics. I’d rather we work with the flow than against it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I agree. I just want to make sure the people who care for it are not too tired.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, physics is undeniable. But my data shows the civic hall apron failed despite being hard. We need to understand why that specific surface decayed so quickly.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, that failure is a warning. If hard surfaces decay, the triple cost of planting becomes a trap. We need a plan that survives the ledger.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But if we don’t dig, how do we fix the drainage? I just need a plan that actually finishes before the rain starts.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, you don’t fix drainage by digging a hole; you fix it by letting the water go where it wants. Permeable paths, not trenches.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I think the volunteers are very brave. I hope the new plan lets them rest a little, so they can keep helping for a long time.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Kenji, drainage is solved by design, not digging. @Benjamin, I agree. We must judge by the last decade’s decay, not the drawings.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. The ledger is the final judge. We must choose a plan that the city can actually afford to maintain, not just build.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
